A||||9||TwisT||Are '88 GT springs different from pre-'88's?  Please post!  ||||1||
Z||000000||TwisT||01-23-2001||10:23 PM||||OK,  here's the deal gang.  I was considering the purchase of the Intraxx springs from Armando,  but there seems to be a debate as to whether the springs will work on all year Fieros.  I want lowering springs for my '88 GT,  but have always thought that the '88's took different springs because of its new suspension.  <P>Intraxx says the springs will work on all '84 to '88 Fieros.  Are they wrong???<P>Thanks for the input!<P>Brett   ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||01-23-2001||11:59 PM||||Unless I miss my guess, the'88's are different.  If someone knows otherwise, please post.  I'd bet the farm on it, though. Does Intrax offer more than one part number? Maybe they have different ones for the '88's.<P>------------------<BR>When you choke a smurf, what color does it turn?||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||01-23-2001||11:59 PM||||Correct me if Im wrong but based on the revised geometry of the strut angles, 84-87 springs shouldn't work on an 88. As for the springs in front I would almost be sure that it would be different as well. <P>According to the 22P parts book there are two different numbers for the seperate suspensions.<P>Always be wary of a counter guy who doesn't know Fieros...||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||01-24-2001||12:05 AM||||'88 springs are different from the earlier years.  I wouldn't buy springs that claim to fit all years......someone didn't do their homework.  Maybe they think all years are the same?  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroMaster88||01-24-2001||01:52 AM||||Does that include the 88 coupe's as well????<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">  <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster86<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles<BR>84 Indy Fiero (restoration Project)||||reg||9
Z||000005||RaeQwan||01-24-2001||02:33 AM||||Yup, us 88's guys get the expensive hard to find stuff for our cars. arn't we lucky  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Ray - AIM: WookieeNC<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ray19nc/" TARGET=_blank>1988 Fiero Coupe</A> - <A HREF="http://www.CarolinaFieros.com" TARGET=_blank>Carolina Fieros</A> - <A HREF="http://www.webjolt.net" TARGET=_blank>WebJolt Network</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfiero||01-24-2001||02:48 AM||||FieroMaster,<P>Yes......that also includes the '88 coupe.  The springs and spring perches on all '88 Fieros are physically different that the earlier years and as such, are not interchangeable (except between other '88s).<P>I have been satisfied with the lowered springs the Fiero Store sells for the '88.  They are $250/set, so they are a bit more expensive than these, but they work!  I've had a set for about 7 years now.||||reg||1
Z||000007||TwisT||01-24-2001||03:33 AM||||Thanks a bunch guys...  I thought I had better varify my hunch before laying down the dough.  Yes,  it's one of those wonderful quirks we '88-owners have to deal with...  special parts required for special cars.  <P>While on the subject...  who else has experience with lowering springs on their '88's?  Curious to see who has what pricing and inches they lower the car.||||reg||1
